# TechJob Analytics — Project Constitution

## Architecture Principles

This project is a **multi-layer data intelligence platform** for the Moroccan IT job market. Raw listings are scraped from ReKrute and Emploi.ma, cleaned and normalized through a Python ETL pipeline into a star schema, served via a FastAPI REST backend, and visualized in both a React dashboard and Power BI. Every layer is independently replaceable. Prefer **simple, explicit data flow** over abstraction layers — the path from CSV → API → chart should be traceable in under 30 seconds of reading. **Convention over configuration**; every file has a single, obvious home.

---

## 1. Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Frontend framework | React 19 with functional components + hooks |
| Build tool | Vite 6 |
| Language | TypeScript 5.8 (strict mode) |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 — utility classes only |
| Routing | react-router-dom v7 |
| Data fetching | @tanstack/react-query v5 (with DevTools) |
| Charts | Recharts v3 |
| Icons | lucide-react (tree-shaken imports) |
| Animations | `motion` v12 |
| Backend API | FastAPI 0.115 (Python) |
| API server | Uvicorn 0.32 |
| Validation | Pydantic v2 |
| Data pipeline | Python (Pandas, NumPy) — Jupyter notebooks |
| Database format | Flat CSV files organized in star schema |
| Reporting | Power BI (`.pbix` files consuming star schema CSVs) |

---

## 2. Conventions

### Folder Structure
```
New_design/
├── src/
│   ├── components/       # One file per React component
│   ├── hooks/            # Custom hooks (especially React Query hooks)
│   ├── lib/              # Library configuration (query client, etc.)
│   ├── types.ts          # All shared TypeScript interfaces
│   ├── data.ts           # Static/mock data and constants
│   ├── App.tsx           # Root component (view router)
│   ├── main.tsx          # Entry point
│   └── index.css         # Tailwind imports + theme tokens
├── backend/              # FastAPI application
│   ├── main.py           # App entry + route definitions
│   └── requirements.txt  # Python dependencies
projet-data-maroc-tech/
├── notebooks/            # Jupyter ETL notebooks
└── data/                 # Raw, clean, and star_schema CSV directories
Kimi_Agent_حذف الأعمدة (1)/  # Data science scripts + Power BI documentation
```

### Naming
- **Components:** PascalCase, default export (`export default function TechJobDashboard`)
- **Hooks:** camelCase with `use` prefix, named export (`export function useGrowthData`)
- **Files:** camelCase for utilities and hooks (`useDashboardData.ts`), PascalCase for components (`TechJobDashboard.tsx`)
- **Types:** PascalCase interfaces in `src/types.ts`
- **API query keys:** camelCase strings matching the resource name (`'growthData'`, `'techRadar'`)

### Code Patterns
- All React Query hooks live in `src/hooks/useDashboardData.ts` — do not create separate hook files for each endpoint
- Components import types from `src/types.ts` and data from `src/data.ts` — never define shared types inside a component file
- Path alias `@/` maps to project root — use for cross-directory imports (`@/components/Foo`), relative imports for same-directory
- Filter state is managed at the dashboard level and passed down as props — no global state store

---

## 3. Constraints (What NOT to Do)

### Frontend
- **No inline styles** — all styling via Tailwind utility classes defined in the theme
- **No state management library** — React built-in state + TanStack Query is sufficient
- **No direct API URL construction outside `useDashboardData.ts`** — all endpoints are centralized there
- **No class components** — functional components + hooks only
- **No CSS modules, styled-components, or Emotion** — Tailwind v4 only
- **No custom CSS class names** — the `@theme` block in `index.css` defines the full design system

### Backend
- **No raw SQL** — the data layer is CSV + Pandas, not a relational database
- **No database connection** — this project serves flat CSV files through FastAPI; do not add PostgreSQL, SQLite, or Supabase unless explicitly directed
- **No ORM imports** — no SQLAlchemy, Prisma, Drizzle, or similar

### Data Pipeline
- **No rewriting the star schema** — it is finalized (9 dims, 1 fact, 3 bridges); extend by adding rows to existing CSVs, not by restructuring
- **No committing large CSVs to git** — data files live on disk, `.gitignore` already excludes them

### General
- **No `any`** — use `unknown` with type narrowing, or define an explicit interface
- **No `// @ts-ignore` or `@ts-expect-error`** — fix the type properly
- **No hardcoded secrets** — `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `APP_URL` are injected via `.env` at runtime
- **No npm packages outside `package.json`** — verify before importing anything new

---

## 4. AI Session Rules

### Before Implementing Anything
1. Read `spec.md` or `requirements.md` if present at project root
2. Read the relevant target file(s) in full before editing
3. Check `src/hooks/useDashboardData.ts` before writing a new data-fetching hook
4. Check `src/types.ts` before defining new interfaces
5. Check `src/components/` before creating a new component (compose or extend first)

### When Ambiguity Arises
STOP. Present exactly **2–3 options** with concrete trade-offs:
- Maintenance burden (will this break on the next dep upgrade?)
- Performance cost (is this adding latency or bundle size?)
- Consistency debt (does this deviate from the existing pattern?)

Do NOT proceed until the user selects one.

### After Implementing
1. Run `npm run lint` (tsc --noEmit) — fix all type errors
2. Run `npm run build` — verify the production bundle compiles
3. Verify backend starts if changes were made to `backend/`
4. Do NOT commit unless explicitly asked

